200
00:15:19,652 --> 00:15:21,012
That's the water chestnuts.

201
00:15:21,632 --> 00:15:26,734
Do you want me to explain?

202
00:15:27,174 --> 00:15:43,840
So the water chestnuts are something that we've been dealing with for many years and the Mystic River Watershed Association is really taking the lead on it and honestly was really starting to get ahead of it and win that battle until the pandemic hit and some of the in-person work

203
00:15:44,552 --> 00:15:47,673
got curtailed, and I think that really set us back.

204
00:15:49,194 --> 00:15:54,256
So the water chestnuts are something that came over from Japan.

205
00:15:54,396 --> 00:16:01,718
They got released out of somebody's oriental garden ages and ages ago, and they do overtake.

206
00:16:02,099 --> 00:16:02,859
It's a problem.

207
00:16:03,299 --> 00:16:11,102
And so typically for many years, the Watershed Association has gotten large grants to pay for a machine

208
00:16:11,666 --> 00:16:19,450
the harvester that comes and takes the water chestnuts off the river and dries, then they dry them out and they compost it.

209
00:16:19,910 --> 00:16:26,534
And the harvester can do most of the river, but it can't pass the Kratik Bridge.

210
00:16:26,574 --> 00:16:28,475
I think that's the point as far as it can go.

211
00:16:29,015 --> 00:16:32,077
So above the Kratik Bridge, it has to be done by hand.

212
00:16:32,697 --> 00:16:36,619
And so they organize events to do hand pulling during the summer.

213
00:16:37,117 --> 00:16:41,966
And the goal is that you have to harvest them before they drop their seeds.

214
00:16:42,507 --> 00:16:45,893
So at this point, it's too late in the season to do anything.

215
00:16:45,913 --> 00:16:47,937
You have to do it earlier in the season.

216
00:16:48,803 --> 00:16:50,444
Oh, no, I appreciate that.

217
00:16:50,684 --> 00:16:58,887
